19:T61d,## Three rules that keep a design lean

These aren’t grand patterns, they’re everyday hygiene. Together they pull in the same direction: **simple, non-duplicated, just-enough** code.

## DRY: Don’t Repeat Yourself

Every piece of knowledge should have **ONE authoritative home**. When the same rule lives in two places, a fix in one copy silently leaves the other wrong:

- A tax formula copy-pasted into `OrderService` *and* `CartService`.
- Fix a rounding bug in one, ship it, and the other still charges wrong.

Extract the shared knowledge into one place both depend on. But beware **over-DRYing**: two pieces of code that merely *look* alike but represent different decisions are not duplication. Coupling them is worse than repeating them.

## KISS: Keep It Simple

The simplest thing that works. **Complexity is a cost, not a badge.** Every abstraction, layer and indirection is something the next reader must hold in their head. Reach for cleverness only when the problem actually demands it.

```
// you needed a counter — you do not need a CounterFactoryStrategy
int count = 0;
```

## YAGNI: You Aren’t Gonna Need It

Don’t build for an imagined future. Speculative flexibility, config you’ll “probably want”, hooks for a feature nobody asked for, is code you maintain forever for a payoff that may never come. Add it **when it’s actually needed**, not before.

> DRY removes duplication, KISS removes complexity, YAGNI removes speculation. Apply all three and what’s left is exactly the code the problem requires, no more, no less.c:["$","div",null,{"className":"flex min-h-screen","children":[["$","$L17",null,{"activeModule":"lld-principles","activeLesson":"dry-kiss-yagni"}],["$","$L18","dry-kiss-yagni",{"lesson":{"id":"dry-kiss-yagni","patternId":"lld-principles","title":"DRY · KISS · YAGNI","kind":"concept","difficulty":"Intro","statement":"Three everyday rules that keep designs lean: Don’t Repeat Yourself, Keep It Simple, You Aren’t Gonna Need It.","companies":["Amazon","Google","Basecamp"],"theory":"$19","approaches":[{"label":"DRY, one source of truth","code":["class OrderService { int calcTax(){ /* … */ } }   // copy","class CartService  { int calcTax(){ /* … */ } }   // paste","","// extract the shared knowledge:","class TaxCalculator { int calc(){ /* … */ } }","// OrderService + CartService now depend on it"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":1,"narration":"OrderService and CartService each carry their OWN copy of calcTax(). The ⧉ marks duplicated knowledge, the same tax rule pasted in two places.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"order","name":"OrderService","methods":["+ calcTax() ⧉"],"x":0,"y":0.3,"tint":"red"},{"id":"cart","name":"CartService","methods":["+ calcTax() ⧉"],"x":1.6,"y":0.3,"tint":"red"}],"relations":[],"shownClassIds":["order","cart"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["order","cart"]},"vars":[["calcTax()","lives in 2 places"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":2,"narration":"Here’s the danger: fix a tax bug in OrderService, ship it, and forget CartService. Now the two copies disagree, and one of them charges customers wrong.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:classes","relations":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:0:steps:0:classDiagram:relations","shownClassIds":["order","cart"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["order","cart"]},"vars":[["fix one copy","other stays buggy 💥"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":5,"narration":"Extract the rule into a single TaxCalculator that both services depend on. One authoritative home, fix it once, everyone gets it. That’s DRY.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"tax","name":"TaxCalculator","methods":["+ calc()"],"x":0.8,"y":0.2,"tint":"green"},{"id":"order2","name":"OrderService","x":0,"y":1.6},{"id":"cart2","name":"CartService","x":1.6,"y":1.6}],"relations":[{"id":"od","from":"order2","to":"tax","kind":"depend","label":"depends on"},{"id":"cd","from":"cart2","to":"tax","kind":"depend","label":"depends on"}],"shownClassIds":["tax","order2","cart2"],"shownRelIds":["od","cd"],"activeIds":["tax"]},"vars":[["calcTax()","one source of truth ✓"]]}]},{"label":"KISS & YAGNI, don’t over-build","code":["// the requirement: render a widget.","// what got built \"in case we need it\":","interface AbstractFactory { … }","class FactoryProvider { … }","class WidgetMgr { … }","// what was actually needed: class Widget { render(); }"],"steps":[{"view":"class","codeLine":3,"narration":"A speculative tower: an AbstractFactory, a FactoryProvider, a WidgetMgr, all built “in case we need it.” For one screen that renders a widget. Nobody asked for any of this.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"mgr","name":"WidgetMgr","x":1,"y":0.2,"tint":"red"},{"id":"absfac","name":"AbstractFactory","stereotype":"interface","x":0,"y":0.2,"tint":"red"},{"id":"provider","name":"FactoryProvider","x":2,"y":0.2,"tint":"red"},{"id":"impl","name":"DefaultWidget","x":1,"y":1.5,"tint":"red"}],"relations":[{"id":"ma","from":"mgr","to":"absfac","kind":"depend"},{"id":"pa","from":"provider","to":"absfac","kind":"depend"},{"id":"ia","from":"impl","to":"absfac","kind":"implement"}],"shownClassIds":["mgr","absfac","provider","impl"],"shownRelIds":["ma","pa","ia"],"activeIds":["absfac","provider"]},"vars":[["classes","4 (for 1 need)"]]},{"view":"class","narration":"Apply KISS + YAGNI: the actual requirement is just “render a widget.” The future this scaffolding prepared for never arrived, so collapse it down to the simplest thing that works.","classDiagram":{"classes":[{"id":"widget","name":"Widget","methods":["+ render()"],"x":1,"y":0.6,"tint":"green"}],"relations":[],"shownClassIds":["widget"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["widget"]},"vars":[["classes","4 → 1 ✓"]]},{"view":"class","codeLine":6,"narration":"One plain Widget with render() does the job. The simplest thing that works, built only when actually needed, add the factories the day a second widget type genuinely shows up, not before.","classDiagram":{"classes":"$c:props:children:1:props:lesson:approaches:1:steps:1:classDiagram:classes","relations":[],"shownClassIds":["widget"],"shownRelIds":[],"activeIds":["widget"]},"vars":[["classes","4 → 1 ✓"],["build it","when needed"]]}]}]}}]]}]
